2026-08-31T18:54Z claude note GOAL 1'S SECOND PERIMETER REVIEW ADDS TWO TERMS HERE (spec/DECISIONS.md 2026-08-31, MVP frame). R4 -- the index answers while it is still filling, its first build included -- and R18 -- an empty answer says whether nothing matched or the scope is not indexed yet -- are now terms of goal 1 with their assertions addressed to this ticket. R4 belongs to the convergence harness, which already drives a build from an empty data directory and polls status: the addition is that queries run against it throughout and are answered. R18's discriminating state is the same harness's partially built index, which is why it lands here rather than in the corpus ticket: the assertion needs a scope that is genuinely not indexed yet, and only a build in progress supplies one. Both decide at BOTH levels under the same ruling's inversion -- the library decides and the fixture stands in for it -- so every assertion this ticket writes for a goal 1 term needs a library-level reading as well as a fixture one
